-- 664_yearround_couple_corridor_seed_repair.sql — year-round COUPLE seeds (goofy / elegant / active dual_scenarios)
-- that stage the couple on a route as a mere stage get a spot in the same place (2026-10-02,
-- NIGHTLY_COMPOSITION_AUDIT_PLAN.md). Pool text only: the couple engine (2026-09-18 restore point) is untouched.
--
-- Why: composition audit: year-round couple seeds that open on a route rendered route-staged 43% vs 10% without.
-- scripts/fix-holiday-corridor-seeds.js --table dual --pools goofy,elegant,active: prefilter 947, judge flagged 246,
-- every rewrite read, ~22 edited by hand (poses the rewriter added taken back out, six invented "fountain rim" spots
-- varied). The dual-swap proximity lint (scripts/lib/posePoolLint.js) run on every rewrite: 0 violations introduced.
-- NOT applied (8): the three wild_rides, the kick-scooter hill, the corn maze (no gain in the 660 test), the bowling
-- strike gag, the rolling library cart gag, and the cherry-blossom bench with a bunny swarm (face swap failed 2/2 in
-- the render test where the original held 2/2).
-- Render test on Kevin's account before any row changed (real nightly-dreams, force_slot_input on his own couple
-- nightlies of the same pool, 12 seeds x 2, original vs rewrite): route-staged 14/24 -> 3/24. Swaps 24/24 vs 21/24:
-- one Fly "Signal timed out" (infra) and the bunny-bench seed 2/2 (excluded). Without that seed and the timeout,
-- identity mean 0.625 vs 0.622 (median 0.635 vs 0.669). Seated 7/24 -> 13/24.
-- Every statement is guarded (still the old text), so a re-run changes nothing.
-- ROLLBACK: swap each statement's SET and WHERE text (the tool's --rollback writes it).

